interpretation:
Slice B adds local proof-level registry / replay guard around the Slice A packet/corridor model.

It proves:
- registry is local proof-only and non-persistent;
- registry is not DRS, not authority, not permission, not Root;
- registry cannot repair invalid packets;
- duplicate packet IDs are rejected;
- duplicate idempotency keys are rejected unless explicit retry-before-terminal-receipt is allowed;
- retry after terminal receipt is rejected;
- expired packet IDs are rejected;
- packet corridor entry validates packet, registry, corridor, and child step;
- packet/corridor mismatch fails closed and returns to Root;
- record_packet_seen returns a new local registry without effects;
- terminal receipt observation records only validated receipt models and creates no receipt, payment, shipment release, permission, or effects;
- reasoning does not restart after Root.

